From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atlas agent <agent@atlas.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:56:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] coherent: a read trap waits for a write running over its
 surface (live surface_coherent_trap_wait=1)

A CPU read trap synced only completed records. While the next frame ran over the surface, its
completion armed the pages again mid-read, and the rest of the read trapped into the newer frame:
one screenshot of two frames, split at a page (simctl io screenshot of a scrolling 3x Simulator,
3 of 18 on 2026-11-14). A read now waits, bounded by surface_coherent_wait_ms and with no group
kept, for running records over the surface, as IOSurfaceLock waits for a Mac GPU's pending writes,
then syncs once. A record held for an event is not waited for (its signal may come from the guest).
Counted: trap_waits, trap_wait_timeouts, trap_wait_ns. Off by default.

Tests (no GPU): tests::coherent_trap_wait, the torn read without the switch and one frame with it.
---
 .../src/shadow_coherent.rs                    | 37 ++++++-
 .../src/tests/coherent_trap_wait.rs           | 98 +++++++++++++++++++
 crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/tests/mod.rs  |  1 +
 3 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/tests/coherent_trap_wait.rs

